for p in pairs:
 a=[r['fractions'][1]['comparisons'][p]['largest_component_share_absolute_change'] for r in rs[1:]];lines.append(f'{p:22s} {100*np.median(a):.1f} percentage points ({100*min(a):.1f} to {100*max(a):.1f})')
lines+=['','Counts of all components, largest-component share, and components needed to cover 90% of selected mass are provided for every mask in selections.csv. No component-size filter was fitted. Tiny quantization speckles affect component counts; bridges can change connectivity abruptly. A change in largest share does not identify which component split or merged, and an unchanged summary does not prove unchanged topology. These are intensity-rank selection effects, not ground-truth errors.','',
'METHOD','Frozen PLAN.json precedes new metrics; SUPPLEMENT_PLAN.json records the later distance-radius addition. Source TIFF and decoded hashes were rechecked against retained PASS receipts, along with valid-mask pins. Source hashes and previous-review provenance are embedded in metrics.json. Native padded alignment [40:2600,200:6920], 20x20 source ownership (IDs 1 or 4 use padded), and published crop [105:2560,380:6021] are unchanged. Region bounds use prior floor/ceil exclusive maxima. Visuals reverse both axes only for published display orientation; calculations use native pixels.','',
'Each map is ranked separately within each support. Therefore a box top-10% mask is not the restriction of the whole-crop top-10% mask. Ranking reduces dependence on differing raw levels but is not calibration or a probability. Fractions 5/10/20% span a small declared high-response grid without tuning to shapes. All boundary ties are included to avoid arbitrary coordinate tie-breaking. Exact-mass weighted Dice uses unit weight above the threshold and a common fractional weight at ties, with min-membership intersection.','']
for q in [.05,.1,.2]:
 a=[f['selections'][n]['selected_fraction'] for r in rs for f in r['fractions'] if f['q']==q for n in f['selections']];lines.append(f'Target {q:.0%}: actual tie-inclusive fraction ranges {min(a):.3%} to {max(a):.3%}.')
a=[abs(m['dice']-m['weighted_dice_exact_mass']) for r in rs for f in r['fractions'] for m in f['comparisons'].values()];lines += [f'Maximum absolute binary-versus-weighted Dice difference over all comparisons: {max(a):.4f}. The full sensitivity grid is retained; no threshold is declared best.','',
'DISTANCE AND CONTROLS','For A-to-B, each selected pixel in A is assigned the Euclidean pixel-center distance to the nearest selected pixel in B within that same support. Reverse distances are pooled with forward distances, including zeros, and mean/p95 computed across the pooled array. Directions are weighted by their selected counts, not averaged equally. Straight lines can cross invalid geometry; these are not geodesic distances. A whole-crop search can find a selected response outside a particular candidate box; a per-box search cannot. Distances are native pixels only, not physical distances, tracked motion, registration shifts, or feature identity. Centroid drift can reflect changing rank prominence or remote components and can conceal local differences.','',
'Self-overlap controls are exactly one; all-box nearest self distances are exactly zero. Uniform-independent occupancy expected Dice 2*pA*pB/(pA+pB) is recorded only as an arithmetic scale (near the selected fraction). Spatial autocorrelation and shared training invalidate treating this as a realistic spatial null, a p-value, or independent evidence. No significance test treats pixels independently.','',
'VERIFICATION AND VISUAL REVIEW','All 342 support/rank/pair overlaps were recomputed from reloaded arrays; an independent cKDTree method reproduced both-direction nearest distances, p95 and centroids for all 324 box comparisons, including the supplemental radius fractions. The whole-crop distance array uses the primary EDT implementation and was not independently recomputed. Component area sums, boundary-rank inequalities, exact weighted mass and source hashes passed. verification.json records the scope. All four generated figures were visually inspected: labels, box inclusion/order, overlap colors and native-aspect-ratio rendering are readable, and the visual pattern agrees with the descriptive numerical results.','',
'LIMITS AND COMPLETION ASSESSMENT','Same saved inputs, model families and shared training create dependent evidence. Quantization, ties, selected fraction, specimen geometry and box clipping affect the summaries. No ground truth, CT-volume reinspection, Hecate map, independent training replication, transcription accuracy, or physical-ink validation is supplied. Reproducible saved-response locations and a completed saved-map analysis do not by themselves finish the four-model reproduction.','',
'FILES','PLAN.json / SUPPLEMENT_PLAN.json: declared analysis scopes','metrics.json: all selections, comparisons, provenance and hashes','comparisons.csv / selections.csv: machine-readable compact tables','all_supports_dice.png: every support and all fractions','all_boxes_overlap_1.png through _3.png: boxes 1-18, all six pair comparisons; phase A=plain/B=padded, cross-model A/B follow name order','analyze.py / verify.py / write_report.py: reproducible code','verification.json: independent numerical-check scope and outcome']
